@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 16
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam dpi 170

title Four-layer standards-traceable architecture and public-run boundary

top to bottom direction

rectangle "External inputs\n\nPublic CIC IoT 2023 flow telemetry\n(source-file cohorts)\n\nISO/IEC 27001:2022: 93 Annex A controls\nNIST CSF 2.0: 106 subcategories\nand official informative references" as inputs #F8F8F8

rectangle "Layer 1: Machine-readable representation\n\nUML/XMI knowledge model for Asset, Event, Threat,\nVulnerability, Control, Metric, and provenance fields" as l1 #E1F5FE

rectangle "Layer 2: Standards mapping and validation\n\nGQM matrix links metrics to ISO/NIST entries.\nValidator checks coverage, broken links, duplicates,\ndangling rows, and official informative-reference consistency.\nBlank templates support future human semantic adjudication." as l2 #F3E5F5

rectangle "Layer 3: Telemetry-derived evidence and risk transformation\n\nFlow-only IDS path, pre-test thresholding,\nisotonic calibration, EP from likelihood plus exploitability prior,\nBR = AV x EP x IL x (1 + wH x HF).\nDeployment enrichment remains an extension hook." as l3 #FFFDE7

rectangle "Layer 4: Portfolio analysis and reporting exports\n\nGordon-Loeb budget, NSGA-II, Greedy-prefix,\nExact-ILP frontiers, artifact-default selector,\nCSV, LaTeX, plots, validator logs." as l4 #E8F5E9

rectangle "Strict public-profile boundary\n\nActivated: telemetry-only evidence path, coverage/integrity/crosswalk validation,\nand frontier-producing portfolio comparison.\n\nNot established: independent semantic correctness, row-varying CVSS exploitability,\nobserved HF effects, auditor/user/tool-level governance reuse." as boundary #FFEBEE

inputs --> l1 : evidence instances
l1 --> l2 : UML class links
l2 --> l3 : validated mapping context
l3 --> l4 : base and residual risk
l4 --> boundary : reported evidence scope

legend bottom
  Solid arrows: activated artifact path in the reported run
  Deployment-only enrichment is documented as an extension hook.
endlegend
@enduml
